  "hypothesis": "Share existing4x4whole-pixel SSE2/AVX2 transpose matrices,32x32scheduling and explicit ownership across all four axis-swapping transforms. Reverse destination-column lanes only for clockwise/transverse; retain measured transpose/counterclockwise kernels and portable tails. One generic row/column-order preparation outside loops, not virtual pixel-loop abstraction. Remove duplicate scalar schedules and allocation/cleanup wrappers when directly superseded.",
  "endState": "One transpose-family ownership entry and shared byte/word/scalar tile schedule, with closed row/column order. Transpose(x,y)->(y,x);CCW->(y,width-1-x);CW->(height-1-y,x);transverse->(height-1-y,width-1-x). Four-lane reversal uses source-derived shuffle0x1b; no channel/alpha interpretation, precision change, extra pass, storage, pool, session, reservation or public API.",
  "scope": "Eight original complete513x259RGBA8/16 axis-swapping transforms with independently owned259x513 outputs. Primary is the demonstrated transverse8 gap. Clockwise/word uncertainties are changed companions, not assumed gaps. Four already passing transpose/CCW costs must be preserved or reconciled; no new fixture, shape/depth/filter grid. Original FFmpeg public transpose graph boundary and exact hiddenRGB/alpha/source/owners/idle-v2/CPU0 remain.",
  "arithmetic": "The0x1bshuffle reverses four complete32/64bit pixels only. Forward-column stores and original row order remain; reverse-column vector start is height-y-row-4. Scalar reversed-tail start is height-y-rows and descending stores cover exactly rows-firstRow cells. No precision/color/alpha operation.",
